---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Funnel from '../components/Funnel.astro';
import Next from '../components/Next.astro';
---
<Base title="Become a maestro — CITY JAM" description="Somebody taught you. Now be the somebody." path="/teach">
  <header class="hero dark bg-deep">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kick"><span class="dot"></span> For people who teach</p>
      <h1>Somebody taught you.<br />Now be the <em>somebody</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every player you have ever loved was taught by someone. That someone is almost never famous. They are the reason anyway. Build one course with us, and teach people who have not been found yet.</p>
      <div class="acts">
        <Funnel funnel="maestroTeachers" campaign="teach" content="apply-as-a-maestro">Apply as a maestro</Funnel>
        <a class="btn ghost lg" href="#how">How it works</a>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Students wait on a different page. <a href="/maestros">Join the class waitlist</a>. No course has launched yet and nobody has been paid yet.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="kick"><span class="dot"></span> The offer, without the dance</p>
      <h2>One subject, yours. Taught your way, built with you.</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li><b>A full course, produced properly.</b> Filmed, edited, structured, hosted. Not a webinar and not a panel.</li>
        <li><b>You earn from it for as long as it earns,</b> on terms written down before you commit an afternoon. The method stays yours.</li>
        <li><b>We market it, and make the promo with you.</b> A few hours of filming together. Not a launch week you run alone.</li>
        <li><b>Students arrive assessed.</b> They got in on their work.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="lead">We are not printing a revenue split. The notes disagree, and a percentage on a public page would pick a side that has not been picked. We bring the audience. That is what our share is for. The number is in the agreement, when there is one, and not before.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="slab" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kick"><span class="dot"></span> What actually happens</p>
      <div class="cards c2">
        <article class="card"><div class="k">01 · You apply</div><h3>Twenty minutes</h3><p>The subject, and a record you made. The record is what we listen to.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><div class="k">02 · We assess the work</div><h3>An hour</h3><p>One conversation to find the actual course. Most people arrive wanting to teach everything and leave with one methodology.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><div class="k">03 · We build it with you</div><h3>A few days, filming</h3><p>You turn up and teach. You are not learning an edit suite at midnight.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><div class="k">04 · It keeps teaching</div><h3>Nothing further from you</h3><p>We keep it in front of artists who arrive, for as long as it is good. The numbers stay open to you.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="kick"><span class="dot"></span> Ways to teach</p>
      <h2>A course. A live masterclass. And room for a format we have not built.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Everything here is digital for now. We will tell you plainly when that changes rather than take a booking for a room that does not exist. Creator Labs is its own programme. It is not a format on this page.</p>
      <p class="lead">Give this a miss if you want a personal brand, if you want income without making anything first, or if you have not made anything in five years. Go and make something, then come back.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="slab">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="kick"><span class="dot"></span> The questions people actually ask</p>
      <h2>Before you apply.</h2>
      <p class="lead"><b>Do I need to be nominated for anything?</b> No. The assessment is the record you send. Plenty of people with a shelf of awards cannot teach.</p>
      <p class="lead"><b>I never went to music school.</b> Neither did most of the people we want. We ask what you have made.</p>
      <p class="lead"><b>I have never taught anything.</b> You have explained this to a bandmate a hundred times. That is teaching. Turning it into a course that holds together is our job.</p>
      <p class="lead"><b>I do not have an audience.</b> Neither do most of the people we are asking. If an audience were the qualification we would end up with the same faculty as everybody else. We bring the audience. That is what our share is for.</p>
      <p class="lead"><b>Do I keep the rights?</b> You keep the method. We licence the course we made together. Not your knowledge.</p>
      <div class="acts" id="fac">
        <Funnel funnel="maestroTeachers" campaign="teach" content="apply">Apply as a maestro</Funnel>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Assessed on the record. Read by a person. An answer either way. If you would rather wait until this is proven, that is fair.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Next items={[
    { href: '/maestros', label: 'For students', note: 'The waitlist. Not this application.' },
    { href: '/labs', label: 'Creator Labs', note: 'Separate. For artists, not faculty.' },
    { href: '/learn', label: 'Learn', note: 'How a visitor finds a class.' },
  ]} />
</Base>
